{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"scratch-files","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Scratch Files","description":"Quick throwaway files for trying code or jotting notes, kept in .ferrum/scratch with a list to find them again.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Productivity"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:scratchFiles.new","onCommand:scratchFiles.newMarkdown","onCommand:scratchFiles.newJavaScript","onCommand:scratchFiles.newPython","onCommand:scratchFiles.fromSelection","onCommand:scratchFiles.open","onCommand:scratchFiles.ignore","onCommand:scratchFiles.forget"],"permissions":["workspace.read","workspace.write"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"scratchFiles.new","title":"New Scratch File...","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.newMarkdown","title":"New Markdown Note","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.newJavaScript","title":"New JavaScript Scratch","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.newPython","title":"New Python Scratch","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.fromSelection","title":"Move Selection to a Scratch File","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.open","title":"Open a Scratch File...","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.ignore","title":"Add Scratch Folder to .gitignore","category":"Scratch Files"},{"command":"scratchFiles.forget","title":"Clear the Scratch List","category":"Scratch Files"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"scratchFiles.new","key":"Ctrl+Alt+N"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Scratch Files: quick throwaway files for trying code or jotting notes. They live in .ferrum/scratch inside your project,\n// so you get full editing, coloring and the terminal. Add that folder to .gitignore if you do not want to commit them.\n\nconst TYPES = [\n  ['Markdown note', 'md'], ['Plain text', 'txt'], ['JavaScript', 'js'], ['TypeScript', 'ts'], ['Python', 'py'], ['JSON', 'json'], ['SQL', 'sql'], ['HTML', 'html'], ['CSS', 'css'],\n  ['Shell', 'sh'], ['Rust', 'rs'], ['Go', 'go'], ['PHP', 'php'], ['YAML', 'yml'],\n];\n\nconst STARTERS = {\n  md: (name) => '# ' + name + '\\n\\n',\n  js: () => \"// Scratch\\nconsole.log('hello');\\n\",\n  ts: () => \"// Scratch\\nconst greet = (name: string) => `Hello, ${name}`;\\nconsole.log(greet('world'));\\n\",\n  py: () => \"# Scratch\\nprint('hello')\\n\",\n  json: () => '{\\n  \\n}\\n',\n  sql: () => '-- Scratch\\nSELECT 1;\\n',\n  html: () => '<!doctype html>\\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n<title>Scratch</title>\\n<p>Hello</p>\\n',\n  css: () => '/* Scratch */\\n',\n  sh: () => '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\n',\n  rs: () => 'fn main() {\\n    println!(\"hello\");\\n}\\n',\n  go: () => 'package main\\n\\nimport \"fmt\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\"hello\")\\n}\\n',\n  php: () => '<?php\\n\\necho \"hello\\\\n\";\\n',\n  yml: () => '# Scratch\\n',\n};\n\nconst DIR = '.ferrum/scratch';\n\nfunction stamp(d = new Date()) {\n  const p = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');\n  return d.getFullYear() + p(d.getMonth() + 1) + p(d.getDate()) + '-' + p(d.getHours()) + p(d.getMinutes()) + p(d.getSeconds());\n}\n\n/** A safe file name stem from what the person typed. */\nfunction stem(name) {\n  return String(name || '').toLowerCase().replace(/\\.[a-z0-9]+$/, '').replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').slice(0, 40);\n}\n\nfunction fileName(name, ext, d) {\n  const s = stem(name);\n  return (s ? s + '-' : 'scratch-') + stamp(d) + '.' + ext;\n}\n\nexports._test = { stamp, stem, fileName, TYPES, STARTERS };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n  const key = () => 'index:' + (ferrum.workspace.root || '');\n\n  async function remember(path, title) {\n    const list = await ferrum.storage.get(key(), []);\n    await ferrum.storage.set(key(), [{ path, title, at: Date.now() }, ...list.filter((x) => x.path !== path)].slice(0, 60));\n  }\n\n  async function create(ext, label) {\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first; scratch files are kept inside it.', 'warn');\n    const title = ((await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Name this scratch file (optional)', placeholder: 'api-test, idea, regex...' })) || '').trim();\n    const path = DIR + '/' + fileName(title, ext);\n    const starter = STARTERS[ext] ? STARTERS[ext](title || 'Scratch') : '';\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(path, starter);\n    await remember(path, title || label);\n    await ferrum.editor.openFile(path);\n  }\n\n  reg('scratchFiles.new', async () => {\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(TYPES.map(([label, ext]) => ({ label, detail: '.' + ext, ext })), { placeholder: 'What kind of scratch file?' });\n    if (pick) await create(pick.ext, pick.label);\n  });\n  for (const [label, ext] of [['Markdown', 'md'], ['JavaScript', 'js'], ['Python', 'py']]) reg('scratchFiles.new' + label, () => create(ext, label));\n\n  reg('scratchFiles.fromSelection', async () => {\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first.', 'warn');\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc || !doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select some text to move into a scratch file.', 'warn');\n    const ext = (doc.name.split('.').pop() || 'txt').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '').slice(0, 6) || 'txt';\n    const path = DIR + '/' + fileName('selection', ext);\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(path, doc.selectedText + '\\n');\n    await remember(path, 'Selection from ' + doc.name);\n    await ferrum.editor.openFile(path);\n  });\n\n  reg('scratchFiles.open', async () => {\n    const list = await ferrum.storage.get(key(), []);\n    if (!list.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No scratch files yet. Run \"Scratch: New Scratch File\".');\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(list.map((x) => ({ label: x.title, detail: x.path, description: new Date(x.at).toLocaleString(), path: x.path })), { placeholder: 'Open a scratch file' });\n    if (!pick) return;\n    try { await ferrum.workspace.readFile(pick.path); } catch {\n      await ferrum.storage.set(key(), list.filter((x) => x.path !== pick.path));\n      return ferrum.window.showMessage('That file no longer exists. It was removed from the list.', 'warn');\n    }\n    await ferrum.editor.openFile(pick.path);\n  });\n\n  reg('scratchFiles.forget', async () => {\n    const list = await ferrum.storage.get(key(), []);\n    if (!list.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The list is already empty.');\n    if (await ferrum.window.confirm('Clear the list of scratch files? The files stay on disk in ' + DIR + '.', 'Clear')) await ferrum.storage.set(key(), []);\n  });\n\n  reg('scratchFiles.ignore', async () => {\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first.', 'warn');\n    let text = '';\n    try { text = await ferrum.workspace.readFile('.gitignore'); } catch { text = ''; }\n    if (/^\\/?\\.ferrum\\/scratch\\/?\\s*$/m.test(text)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('.gitignore already ignores the scratch folder.');\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile('.gitignore', text + (text && !text.endsWith('\\n') ? '\\n' : '') + '.ferrum/scratch/\\n');\n    ferrum.window.showMessage('Added .ferrum/scratch/ to .gitignore.');\n  });\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Scratch Files\n\nCreate a throwaway file in a second: **New Scratch File...** asks for a kind (Markdown, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, JSON, SQL, HTML, CSS, shell, Rust, Go, PHP, YAML, text) and an optional name, writes a starter, and opens it. You get full coloring, the terminal and every other feature, because it is a real file.\n\n- Files live in `.ferrum/scratch/` inside your project, with the time in the name so they never collide.\n- **Open a Scratch File...** lists the ones you made for this project, newest first.\n- **Move Selection to a Scratch File** takes the selected text out of what you are editing.\n- **Add Scratch Folder to .gitignore** keeps them out of your commits.\n\nFerrum cannot delete files for an extension, so scratch files stay on disk until you delete them in the file explorer.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**workspace.read** and **workspace.write**, to create and open the files. Only inside the folder you opened.\n"}}}